  Version 20261114~sparky9~0 (2026-11-14)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  * ORDER 572: a fresh install boots clean. A step right after the fstab step, shellprocess@cushionswap, hands the
    swap area the installer made to Cushion Swap (cushion-swap --adopt installer, in the new system): its line in
    /etc/fstab is marked noauto, so the area is off at boot and Cushion Swap has its area from the first boot
    (Daniel's design: swap off until memory runs short). An install on a real notebook had reported "no swap area is
    configured". Hibernation resumes from the same area as before.
  * The dual-boot step turns os-prober on for any other system it finds, Windows or another Linux, so GRUB lists it
    and sparky-stereo-boot shows the menu (Daniel, 2026-10-07: "dual boot found at install: os-prober on and menu
    shown; single OS: os-prober off, menu hidden"); the local-time clock stays for Windows only.

